    {
      "text": "kingdoms of the world, and the glory of them, Matt. 4:8. that they may have glory of men, Matt. 6:2. thine is the kingdom, and the power, and the glory, Matt. 6:13. seeketh his own glory, John 7:18. because he gave not God the glory, Acts 12:23. let no man glory in men, 1 Cor. 3:21. long hair, it is a glory to her, 1 Cor. 11:15. one star differeth from another star in glory, 1 Cor. 15:41 (D&C 76:81, 98). not steadfastly behold the face of Moses for the glory of his countenance, 2 Cor. 3:7. affliction … worketh for us a far more exceeding and eternal weight of glory, 2 Cor. 4:17 (D&C 63:66). whose glory is in their shame, Philip. 3:19. riches of the glory of this mystery, Col. 1:27. ye also appear with him in glory, Col. 3:4. Nor of men sought we glory, 1 Thes. 2:6. received up into glory, 1 Tim. 3:16. glory not, and lie not against the truth, James 3:14. rejoice with joy unspeakable and full of glory, 1 Pet. 1:8. all the glory of man as the flower of grass, 1 Pet. 1:24. a partaker of the glory that shall be revealed, 1 Pet. 5:1. shall receive a crown of glory, 1 Pet. 5:4. hath called us unto his eternal glory by Christ, 1 Pet. 5:10. him that hath called us to glory and virtue, 2 Pet. 1:3. he received from God the Father honour and glory, 2 Pet. 1:17. Fear God, and give glory to him, Rev. 14:7.",
